-- title:
--   Double-annihilator property of the twisted pairing on J_H(M)[n]
-- statement:
--   Fix a natural number $M\neq 0$, a subgroup $H\le(\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$ and a natural number $n\neq 0$. Write $JH\,M\,H$ for the degree-zero divisor class group $\mathrm{Pic}^{0}$ of the function field of $X_H$ base changed to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, i.e. of `xHFunctionFieldBar M H`, the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-subfield of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-Laurent series generated by the coefficientwise image of `xHFunctionField M H`. The assertion is that there exists a function $B : JH\,M\,H \times JH\,M\,H \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ such that, for all $x,y$ killed by $n$: $B(x,y)^{n}=1$; $B$ is additive in each argument (on elements killed by $n$); $B$ is non-degenerate in the first argument, i.e. $B(x,\cdot)\equiv 1$ on the $n$-torsion forces $x=0$; for every $\sigma\in\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ and every $c$ coprime to $M$ with $\sigma\zeta=\zeta^{c}$ for all $\zeta$ with $\zeta^{M}=1$, one has $B(\langle c\rangle(\sigma\cdot x),\sigma\cdot y)=\sigma(B(x,y))$, where $\langle c\rangle$ is `diamondHBar M H` at the unit determined by $c$, the endomorphism of $\mathrm{Pic}^{0}$ induced by the chosen automorphism `diamondAutHBar`; for every prime $\ell$ the endomorphism `heckeOperatorHAlong (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) M H ℓ` is self-adjoint for $B$, and so is $\langle d\rangle$ for every $d\in(\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$; $B$ is also non-degenerate in the second argument; and finally, for every additive subgroup $A\le JH\,M\,H$ all of whose elements are killed by $n$, any $n$-torsion $x$ with $B(x,y)=1$ for every $n$-torsion $y$ annihilating $A$ lies in $A$ — that is, $A$ equals its double annihilator inside the $n$-torsion.
--
--   This is the Weil/Cartier pairing on the $n$-torsion of the Jacobian of $X_H$, twisted by a diamond operator so that the Hecke operators and the diamonds become self-adjoint rather than adjoint to their transposes, together with the statement that annihilation with respect to it is an involution on subgroups of the $n$-torsion. It strengthens the pairing produced by [`ModularCurve.exists_pairing_nsmul_eq_zero_galois_heckeH_diamondH`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_pairing_nsmul_eq_zero_galois_heckeH_diamondH) by right non-degeneracy and the double-annihilator identity, and is used by [`ModularCurve.exists_bilinForm_torsion_jH_nondegenerate_genOpH_selfAdjoint_galois`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_bilinForm_torsion_jH_nondegenerate_genOpH_selfAdjoint_galois) in the analysis of Galois- and Hecke-stable subgroups of $J_H(M)[p]$.
